  "name": "Bays of Vietnam (Vịnh biển Việt Nam)",
  "title": "Bays of Vietnam (Vịnh biển Việt Nam)",
  "description": "Catalog of named bays and gulfs (vịnh) and coves (vũng) along the Vietnamese coastline, including UNESCO World Heritage Site Hạ Long Bay, the adjacent Bái Tử Long, the strategic Cam Ranh deep-water bay, Nha Trang, Đà Nẵng, Vân Phong, and 17 others. Each record carries Wikidata QID, native Vietnamese name plus English/French/Chinese/Japanese/Korean/Thai/German/Spanish/Portuguese/Russian names where available, descriptions in Vietnamese/English/French, country (P17), instance-of types (P31), administrative location (P131), parent water body (P206 — typically South China Sea / Biển Đông), coordinates (P625), area (P2046), length (P2043), max depth (P4511), and Commons image URL (P18), plus Wikipedia sitelinks for 11 languages.",
